config ZMK_INPUT_PROCESSOR_REL_THROTTLE
    bool "Relative-motion report throttle input processor"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_ZMK_INPUT_PROCESSOR_REL_THROTTLE_ENABLED
    help
      Coalesces relative pointing-device motion so at most one HID report per
      interval is sent, while keeping every reported delta (nothing is
      dropped). The interval is selected at runtime from the active endpoint
      transport, so USB can stay unthrottled while BLE is throttled enough for
      the HID-over-GATT report queue to keep up.

      Place it first in a zmk,input-listener input-processors chain, and in the
      listener's base config as well as any layer overrides, since a matching
      override with process-next unset does not fall through to the base chain.
